      "uz_compare": "O'zbekchada 'ishladi' o'rniga hurmat bilan 'ishladilar' yoki 'ishlagan edilar' deymiz. Koreyschada: 일했어요 → 일하셨어요.",
      "compare_en": "English past tense is the same for everyone: 'my father worked', 'I worked'. Korean adds honorific -(으)시- before the past ending when the subject deserves respect: 일했어요 → 일하셨어요."
    },
    {
      "id": "u01_l2_g2",
      "pattern": "A/V-고",
      "meaning_uz": "Sanash: '... va ...', '...-ib'",
      "meaning_en": "Listing: 'and'",
      "explanation_md": "**-고** — ikki va undan ko'p **xususiyat yoki harakat**ni **sanab** bog'laydi: o'zbekchadagi **\"va\"**, **\"...-ib\"**.\n\n**아버지는 조용하고 친절하세요.** — *Otam jim va mehribonlar.*\n\n### Qanday yasaladi\n\nO'zakka **-고** qo'shiladi, 받침ga qarab o'zgarmaydi:\n\n- 크다 → **크고**\n- 친절하다 → **친절하고**\n- 좋다 → **좋고**\n- 맛있다 → **맛있고**\n\n**Ot** bilan: **N이고** (받침 bor), **N고** (받침 yo'q):\n\n형은 회사원**이고** 누나는 의사**예요**.\n\n### Ikki xil gap\n\n1. Bitta odam haqida ikki xususiyat:\n   - 이 식당은 싸**고** 맛있어요. — *Bu restoran arzon va mazali.*\n2. Ikki odam haqida taqqoslab:\n   - 아버지는 엄하시**고** 어머니는 친절하세요.\n\n### Zamon\n\nZamon odatda **oxirgi fe'l**da: 키가 크**고** 멋있**었어요**.\n\n### Diqqat\n\n**-고** dan oldin **-아/어** qo'shilmaydi: ~~커고~~ ❌ → **크고** ✅",
      "explanation_md_en": "**-고** joins two or more **qualities or actions** in a list, like English **\"and\"**.\n\n**아버지는 조용하고 친절하세요.** — *My father is quiet and kind.*\n\n### How to form it\n\nAdd **-고** to the stem; it does not change with 받침:\n\n- 크다 → **크고**\n- 친절하다 → **친절하고**\n- 좋다 → **좋고**\n- 맛있다 → **맛있고**\n\nWith a **noun**: **N이고** (with 받침), **N고** (no 받침):\n\n형은 회사원**이고** 누나는 의사**예요**.\n\n### Two kinds of sentence\n\n1. Two qualities of one person or thing:\n   - 이 식당은 싸**고** 맛있어요. — *This restaurant is cheap and tasty.*\n2. Comparing two people:\n   - 아버지는 엄하시**고** 어머니는 친절하세요.\n\n### Tense\n\nThe tense usually goes on **the last verb** only: 키가 크**고** 멋있**었어요**.\n\n### Watch out\n\nDo not add **-아/어** before **-고**: ~~커고~~ ❌ → **크고** ✅",
      "formation": [
        {
          "condition_uz": "Fe'l / sifat",
          "condition_en": "Verb / adjective",
          "rule": "-고",
          "example": "크다 → 크고, 친절하다 → 친절하고"
        },
